--
N5008 [temp.variadic]/5 + [expr.prim.fold]: a fold pattern that is a
QUALIFIED reference to a member of each pack element (`Ts::v`) keeps its
trailing components across substitution.  The class-body fold expander
used to replace the whole qualified name with the element type, so
`static inline int value = (Ts::v + ...)` became a bare type expression
and symex CRASHED (invariant "assignments must be type consistent").
Static constexpr members with the same fold took a different, working
path, masking the defect.  Found by feature-sweep defect hunting;
header-free; g++/clang++ runtime-verified.
